  "historical_output_text": " Task explanation - changing a ceiling lamp:\nPreparing to perform routine home ceiling-lamped changing is straightforward but safety and organization is paramount. Ensure no electrical work or maintenance has already occurred. Turn on lights to check which one requires changing. Ensure all necessary replacement and replacement lamp hardware or bulbs is within arms-reachable reach of the lamp or at an accessible level in an electrical cabinet/pan. Gather and place on stable workbench. \nRemove all hardware (bushings or other securing pieces) to gain full, secure grip of light. Unsheat the wire insulation to reach the screws securing the fixture and loosen the fixture by turning counteraiclockise to disconnect from ceiling wires.\nLiberate light and place onto work area, unsheaten the wiring and check if there’s enough slack or wiring needs replacement if not secure. Insert the replacement into wires",
